{#-
  One article, as a row. Expects `post` in scope.

  Shared by /insights/ and the tag archives so the two cannot drift. They had
  already drifted once: the tag pages were using a class called
  insight-card-body that had no rule anywhere in the stylesheet, so the same
  three articles were spaced properly on the index and collided on a tag page.
  One row, one partial, one set of rules.

  The picture link is hidden from assistive technology and taken out of the tab
  order. It goes to the same place as the headline directly beside it, so a
  screen reader would otherwise announce every article twice and a keyboard
  user would tab twice to move one row. The headline is the real link, and the
  alt text still describes the picture to anyone who has images turned off.
-#}
{#- data-tags carries every tag, not just the one shown as the kicker, so the
    filter matches an article on any of its topics rather than only on whichever
    happened to be listed first in the front matter. Delimited with pipes and
    padded at both ends so a match on "|News|" cannot also hit "Company News". -#}
<article class="insight-row{% if not post.data.image %} insight-row--noimage{% endif %}"
         data-tags="|{% for tag in post.data.tags %}{{ tag }}|{% endfor %}">
  {% if post.data.image %}
  <a class="insight-row-image" href="{{ post.url }}" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">
    <img src="{{ post.data.image }}" alt="{{ post.data.image_alt or post.data.title }}" loading="lazy">
  </a>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="insight-row-text">
    {%- if post.data.tags and post.data.tags.length %}
    {%- set kicker = post.data.tags[0] %}
    {#- A link only where the tag actually has an archive page. Below the
        three-article threshold in .eleventy.js there is no page to send anyone
        to, and a kicker that looks like a link and is not is worse than one
        that never claimed to be. -#}
    {%- if kicker in collections.tagsWithPages %}
    <a class="insight-row-kicker" href="/insights/tag/{{ kicker | tagSlug }}/">{{ kicker }}</a>
    {%- else %}
    <span class="insight-row-kicker">{{ kicker }}</span>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}
    <h2><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></h2>
    <time datetime="{{ post.date | date('%Y-%m-%d') }}">{{ post.date | date('%d %b %Y') }}</time>
  </div>
</article>
